---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'
import { pricing, formatPrice } from '@/data/pricing'
import { release } from '@/data/release'
import { site } from '@/data/site'
---

<Base
  title="Hero Notch terms of use & licensing"
  description="Plain-language terms for buying, downloading, and using the Hero Notch macOS and Windows desktop workspace."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Terms &amp; License</span>
      <h1>Terms, in plain language.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Short version: one payment, a lifetime Notch v1 license with no recurring subscription, and
        local-first ownership of your files.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. One-time license &amp; pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Hero Notch is a macOS and Windows desktop application licensed through a one-time payment — never a
        subscription. The launch price is <strong>{formatPrice(pricing.earlyBird.price)}</strong> for
        the first <strong>{pricing.earlyBird.seats} licenses</strong> (Early Bird) and
        <strong>{formatPrice(pricing.standard.price)}</strong> afterwards (Standard). Early buyers
        keep their launch price permanently; subsequent price transitions never apply retroactively.
        Every license unlocks all workspace modules (Notes Vault, Music, Planner &amp; Google
        Calendar, AI Sessions, Posture Coach, Local Wi-Fi Phone Transfer, and Hydration + Focus
        Timer) and includes all Notch v1.x updates.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Final sale &amp; no-refund policy</h2>
      <p>
        Because Hero Notch issues your permanent Early Bird license key immediately upon prebooking,
        all purchases are final and non-refundable. Both MacBook (macOS) and Windows builds are
        currently coming soon and will unlock with your license key at launch. For questions or
        support, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What your license allows</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Install and use Hero Notch on any MacBook (macOS) and Windows 10 or Windows 11 computers
          that you personally own or use for your work.
        </li>
        <li>
          Connect Hero Notch to any local Markdown or Obsidian vaults for personal or commercial
          writing, engineering, and planning.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not resell, sublicense, bypass payment gates, or publicly redistribute license keys or
          paid installer binaries.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Local files &amp; third-party integrations</h2>
      <p>
        Notch edits plain Markdown (<code>.md</code>) and text (<code>.txt</code>) files directly
        inside the folder you select. While deletions from the Notch file tree use the Windows
        Recycle Bin and saves are atomic, you remain responsible for backing up your local vaults.
      </p>
      <p>
        Notch interoperates with third-party software and services — including Obsidian, Spotify,
        Google Calendar, OpenAI Codex, OpenCode, Google Anti Gravity, and Anthropic Claude Code —
        but is an independent product and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those providers.
        When you use optional OAuth connections or send a prompt to a local coding CLI, the
        respective provider’s terms of service and privacy policy apply.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Webcam posture coach &amp; hydration reminders</h2>
      <p>
        The on-device posture coach and hydration tracker are ergonomic and habit-awareness aids,
        not medical devices. They do not provide medical diagnosis, physical therapy, or clinical
        advice.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Warranty disclaimer &amp; installer verification</h2>
      <p>
        Hero Notch is provided “as-is” without warranty of any kind. Independent desktop releases may
        trigger standard macOS Gatekeeper or Windows SmartScreen confirmation on first launch; every
        licensed installer package includes an integrity checksum on your delivery receipt.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Updates to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as new Notch releases ship. Updates never alter the one-time nature
        of your existing license or increase a price you have already paid. Questions? Contact
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
